    <DataNode elementId="AT5G08280-MONOMER" textLabel="hydroxymethylbilane synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q43316" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Porphobilinogen deaminase (PBG deaminase) has been purified to homogeneity from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; extracts (16,000-fold) |CITS:[8192681]|. The protein was shown to be monomeric and to contain a dipyrromethane cofactor attached covalently to an invariant cysteine (Cys-242 in the &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; orthologue, Cys-254 in the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; protein). &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; PBG deaminase exhibits a broad pH optimum between 7.7 and 8.5. The enzyme shows remarkable thermal stability with little loss of activity after heating to 70 ºC |CITS:[8192681]|. A number of inhibitors (see below) have been identified. Notably, NH&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; (tested in the form of NH&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt;Cl) , a product of deamination was shown to inhibit PBG deaminase activity. All the prophyrins and porphyrinogens tested also inhibited activity to some extent (5-15%), but none were highly inhibitory |CITS:[8192681]|. Another study isolated the gene (&lt;i&gt;HEMC&lt;/i&gt;) encoding the enzyme |CITS:[8000000]|. N-terminal sequencing of the purified enzyme indicates that the purified protein is highly likely to be encoded by &lt;i&gt;HEMC&lt;/i&gt; |CITS:[8000000],[8192681]|. The product of this gene was shown to be nuclear-encoded, and bound to the chloroplast |CITS:[8000000]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G08280-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G08280.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Swissmodel" value="Q43316" />
