    <DataNode elementId="AT1G50170-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G50170-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G50170-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding sirohydrochlorin ferrochelatase (AtSirB) has been identified and characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The molecular function of inserting ferrous ion into sirohydrochlorin to generate siroheme has been proven by functional complementation of a sirohydrochlorin ferrochelatase deficient strain of &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; and by characterizing the purified, recombinant protein expressed in this bacterium. AtSirB has an integral Fe-S center which has been discussed in terms of a close association with the metabolism of sulfur and iron.The subcellular location in the chloroplast has been determined by confocal microscopy using a GFP-fusion protein in transgenic tobacco leaf cells. The characterization of sirohydrochlorin ferrochelatase underlines the involvement of single enzymes to each step of the siroheme biosynthesis and distinguishes this process in plants from the otherwise exact reaction sequence observed in some bacteria |CITS: [15545265]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G50170-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-9640" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G50170.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G50170" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="15545265" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15545265" />
    </DataNode>
